__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
.env
.env.local
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
state/*.db
state/*.db-journal
# Stray runtime state written OUTSIDE the root state/ dir. The db helpers
# mkdir their parent relative to the PROCESS cwd, so running a query from
# inside e.g. a direction dir scaffolds an empty `state/factory.db` there and it
# gets committed as a binary. The rules above are root-anchored by design; this
# one has to be recursive to catch the accidents.
**/state/*.db
**/state/*.db-journal
state/dry_run_scratch/
# Per-story event logs (JSONL, append-only, grow with chain activity).
# Surface via ``factory why`` / ``factory trace``; recreated on demand.
state/logs/
# Factory-improver proposal JSONs. Each ``factory improve`` run writes
# one; surfaced via the pinned GH issue and the L2 apply pass — durable
# state lives in the PRs that result, not here.
state/improvements/
# Event-trigger debounce / daily-cap history for the factory_improver
# (one ISO timestamp per fire, pruned to 24h). Pure runtime bookkeeping.
state/.improver_run_history.json
# Per-story git worktrees created by factory.chain.worktree. Each is a
# linked working dir under state/worktrees/<app>-<id>-<slug>/; sharing
# .git with the source app repo, NOT this one.
state/worktrees/
# FMS Phase-1 structured event streams (append-only NDJSON). Runtime-only;
# read via ``factory manager signals dump``. Do NOT commit .ndjson files.
state/events/
# FMS runtime telemetry — concern documents (L2) and diagnosis proposals
# (L3). Append-only runtime artifacts; the durable record is the PRs/issues
# they produce. Read via ``factory manager ...`` CLI, never from git.
state/concerns/
state/manager_proposals/
# Post-merge context-refresh scratch worktrees.
state/context-refresh/
# WS1.2 independent acceptance oracles — spec-derived acceptance tests authored
# at story spawn and stored per-story under state/acceptance/<app>/<id>/. Runtime
# artifacts kept OUT of the app repo AND the dev worktree so the dev never sees
# them; the durable record is the merge gate result, not git.
state/acceptance/
# Per-app machine-writable runtime overrides (factory.runtime_state). Holds
# machine flips like deploy_enabled that used to be written into config.yaml
# in-place — split out so operator-authored config.yaml is never machine-
# mutated and the two never drift. Runtime-only; config.yaml is the durable
# operator default.
state/runtime/
# Halt/apply audit trails — runtime bookkeeping mutated by every
# halt/resume/apply cycle; ``factory resume`` archives into them.
state/.halt_history.json
state/.manager_apply_history.json
state/.improver_backoff.json
state/*.log
# Timestamped SQLite snapshots taken before destructive repairs (``state/*.db``
# is already ignored; the ``.bak-<epoch>`` copies are the same data and run to
# tens of MB each). Recovery artifacts, never part of the durable record.
state/*.db.bak-*
# L1 idle-generator bookkeeping — last-fire timestamp so the idle loop does not
# re-fire within its cooldown. Pure runtime; recreated on demand.
state/idle_generator.json
# Manager escalation debounce history (one entry per L2->L3 escalation, pruned
# on read). Runtime-only; the durable record is the concern/proposal PRs.
state/.manager_escalation_history.json
# Issue-hygiene watermarks (``<app>.last``) — the reconcile pass stores the last
# swept cursor per app so it does not rescan closed issues every tick.
state/issue_hygiene/

# Diff-scoped mutation scores, one file per (app, head_sha): the durable record
# of a ``factory mutation-score`` run AND its per-symbol cache, without which a
# re-measurement costs one full test-suite run per symbol. Runtime, per-checkout.
state/mutation/

# Claude Code agent worktrees — linked working dirs sharing this repo's .git,
# created per background agent and removed when unchanged. Never committed.
# (``.claude/skills/`` IS tracked: those are checked-in project skills.)
.claude/worktrees/

# Direction artifacts — mockups, screen recordings, binaries a persona was given
# as input. Keep them on disk next to their direction, but NEVER in git: three
# exercise-demo mp4s put 50 MB into this repo's history permanently (git's pack
# is 72 MB, almost all of it those files). Text siblings (direction.md, flow.md,
# api_spec.md) are the reviewable source and stay tracked.
#
# Already-committed binaries are NOT removed by this rule — history still holds
# them, and rewriting it would invalidate every open branch and PR. This stops
# the bleeding; use git-lfs or object storage if you need new large inputs.
apps/*/directions/*/artifacts/**
!apps/*/directions/*/artifacts/.gitkeep

# Machine-written direction state (direction 018). Direction 012 made the
# ``directions`` TABLE authoritative for a direction's status; ``state.yaml`` is
# now a projection the chain rewrites on every transition. It is still WRITTEN to
# disk so an operator can read a status without querying the database, but it
# must never be tracked: a tick that changes a status has to leave the tree
# clean. ``factory directions-regenerate-state`` rebuilds it in a fresh clone.
#
# The human-authored siblings (direction.md, flow.md, api_spec.md) are the
# reviewable source and stay tracked — only ``state.yaml`` is machine-written.
apps/*/directions/*/state.yaml

# Machine-written story markdown (direction 018). ``stories.sm_result_json`` is
# the source of truth; the rendered markdown is a projection nothing reads out of
# git. Two patterns, because the chain writes the file twice under two roots:
#   * apps/<app>/stories/<id>-<slug>.md — where the SM handler writes it
#     (``software_factory_root / "apps" / app / target_path``).
#   * stories/<id>-<slug>.md — the SAME relative target_path the dev persona is
#     handed, resolved against ITS worktree root. For the ``factory`` app that
#     worktree shares this repo, so the copy lands at the repo root and the dev
#     commits it. This was the dominant leak: nearly every merged story PR
#     added one.
# Both patterns contain a slash, so both are anchored to their own directory —
# nothing outside them is affected, and non-``.md`` files in them stay tracked.
apps/*/stories/*.md
stories/*.md

# coverage.py data file (never commit)
.coverage

# SWE-bench harness scratch: per-run clones, worktrees, docker logs and diffs.
# The manifest, selftest verdicts and results.md ARE tracked — they are the
# evidence. `runs/` is 350MB+ of reproducible working data and is not.
# `results-archive/` is deliberately NOT ignored: `report` snapshots the
# small per-row evidence files (result.json/audit.json/prediction.diff)
# there so every published table stays backed by committed artifacts.
bench/swebench/runs/

# Phase-0 staging backups (bench/swebench/phase0_sail_ab.py p0_4-stage). Full
# copies of real run dirs, including grade.log / grade-nodes.log — the hidden
# test ids the record store marks answer_key and that `export` refuses to emit.
bench/swebench/.phase0-backups/

# selftest per-instance rows are the parallel driver INTERMEDIATE; `selftest.json`
# is the artifact they merge into and the one source of truth the sweep reads.
bench/swebench/selftest-rows/

# The benchmark RECORD store's WAL sidecars — transient by definition, recreated
# on every open, and meaningless without the db. `benchmarks.db` itself is
# deliberately NOT ignored: it is the ONLY place a superseded attempt's figures
# survive (`runs/` above is wiped by the next attempt of the same cell), so
# ignoring it would put the durable record in the one directory git cannot see.
# See bench/swebench/BENCHMARK-RECORDS.md.
bench/swebench/benchmarks.db-wal
bench/swebench/benchmarks.db-shm

# The benchmark record store is REGENERABLE from results-archive/ (proven:
# `benchmark_store ingest --runs-dir <archive> --swe-dir <archive>` rebuilds it
# and `verify` reports 176 ok / 0 gone / 0 MISMATCH). Keeping the binary out of
# git avoids two problems: opaque diffs and merge conflicts on a sqlite file,
# and a pre-existing hole where `record()`/`_record_sweep()` do not thread
# db_path, so ANY test run writes campaign/ingest_log rows into the committed
# copy. The archive is the source of truth; this is the queryable index.
bench/swebench/benchmarks.db

# dev-tools import (2026-11-06): this tree lives in a PUBLIC repo. Only the
# factory's own app configs are tracked; every other registered app (INNERGY
# repos included) stays local to the factory machine and is never committed.
apps/*
!apps/factory/
!apps/template-probe/

# JOBS-API v1.2 runtime: research/report jobs (job.yaml, report.md, workspaces)
# and Claude Code run dirs (round scripts, stream-json). Runtime-only; read via
# ``factory job status|report``.
state/jobs/
state/claude_runs/
# Directions the factory files and runs are machine-written runtime state
# (direction 018): already-tracked ones stay tracked, new ones are never added.
apps/factory/directions/
apps/template-probe/directions/
